WEBVTT

00:01.530 --> 00:04.080
AKASAKA
DOJO

00:15.960 --> 00:16.010
PEACE ABOVE ALL

00:24.980 --> 00:26.840
Indeed...

00:27.880 --> 00:33.280
our tiny neighborhood has no need for two dojos, Mr. Akasaka.

00:33.770 --> 00:35.820
So what are you suggesting?

00:36.650 --> 00:41.620
Starting  today,  I'll!!

00:36.900 --> 00:41.620
Presented by Saizen-Yabai

01:50.440 --> 01:52.830
What the? Dammit!

01:52.830 --> 01:55.910
Take this, bitches!

01:55.910 --> 01:57.230
Dammit!

01:57.230 --> 01:58.190
You get him?

01:58.910 --> 02:00.930
You didn't hit us!

02:00.930 --> 02:02.770
It's on now! Oops!

02:05.960 --> 02:07.250
Think fast!

02:13.510 --> 02:17.090
Mitsuhashi! Packing in rocks is cheating, asshole!

02:18.180 --> 02:20.930
Quit bitching over a fucking pebble!

02:21.250 --> 02:23.210
How the hell is <i>that a pebble!</i>

02:23.210 --> 02:25.970
Mitsuhashi! You'd even cheat in a snowball fight?!

02:27.660 --> 02:28.640
D-Dammit!

02:29.790 --> 02:31.100
Come and get me!

02:30.810 --> 02:31.820
Asswipe!

02:31.100 --> 02:33.000
Over here!

02:33.420 --> 02:35.380
That missed me by a mile, loser!

02:35.380 --> 02:37.070
You suck balls!

02:37.070 --> 02:39.950
Where were you aiming at! You fucking blow!

02:37.070 --> 02:38.410
Guys!

02:38.410 --> 02:39.950
I thought you were supposed to be cleaning!

02:40.410 --> 02:41.360
Crap.

02:41.360 --> 02:44.540
If you want to play, finish cleaning first!

02:44.540 --> 02:46.020
Honestly, you guys...

02:46.700 --> 02:48.500
Take that stick outta your ass!

02:48.500 --> 02:52.040
Snow in the city is just like pleasure: they melt away too fast!

02:52.520 --> 02:53.890
H-Hey!

02:53.890 --> 02:54.750
Three! What—

02:57.030 --> 02:58.020
Riko!

02:58.580 --> 03:00.380
You all right, Riko?

03:04.340 --> 03:07.810
Did that idiot Mitsuhashi hide rocks in those snowballs?

03:07.810 --> 03:09.180
Are you all right, Riko?

03:09.180 --> 03:11.670
I-I'm all right, don't worry about me.

03:11.670 --> 03:13.770
I just slipped on the snow.

03:14.110 --> 03:15.580
It's still Mitsuhashi's fault.

03:15.580 --> 03:17.650
God, he always takes things too far.

03:17.650 --> 03:19.730
Let's take you to the nurse's office!

03:19.730 --> 03:21.560
Here, grab my hand.

03:21.560 --> 03:24.760
I-It ain't my fault. I didn't do nothing.

03:27.050 --> 03:29.290
What? The fuck y'all looking at?

03:30.450 --> 03:30.490
Bombing on a
Dojo Challenge!!

03:37.000 --> 03:40.530
Riko, are you sure you don't want to go to a hospital?

03:40.530 --> 03:43.500
I'm fine. I only twisted it a little.

03:43.500 --> 03:44.980
Really?

03:46.280 --> 03:48.600
Christ, talk about high maintenance!

03:48.430 --> 03:48.470
AKASAKA
DOJO

03:55.760 --> 03:59.010
Do you live here, Riko? Wow...

03:59.010 --> 04:01.130
It <i>is an old and storied dojo.</i>

04:01.130 --> 04:03.460
Her family has owned it for many generations.

04:03.460 --> 04:05.530
It's just an old place.

04:05.530 --> 04:09.610
Why's everyone else's familes loaded except mine?

04:09.610 --> 04:11.570
I'll go call our master!

04:11.570 --> 04:13.540
You guys can come in.

04:30.800 --> 04:32.850
This is tight.

04:32.850 --> 04:38.140
Your ancestors must've done some illegal shit if they built a crib this big.

04:38.140 --> 04:38.810
That's stupid!

04:40.960 --> 04:42.780
These are some huge goldfish!

04:43.090 --> 04:44.890
Those are colored carp.

04:44.890 --> 04:48.610
They're very expensive. One can run you millions of yen.

04:51.260 --> 04:52.370
Put it back!

04:52.370 --> 04:52.950
Right.

04:54.420 --> 04:57.200
Man, this tree's all bendy and shit!

04:57.200 --> 05:00.040
What the hell got you all twisted, huh?

05:00.040 --> 05:02.470
It's as twisted as your personality.

05:02.470 --> 05:04.480
That's also expensive.

05:05.100 --> 05:06.010
Hey!

05:06.850 --> 05:08.360
Stop this instant!

05:08.360 --> 05:09.200
Okay!

05:09.200 --> 05:10.730
Master, this way!

05:12.260 --> 05:13.390
R-Riko!

05:13.390 --> 05:14.930
Are you really injured?!

05:16.410 --> 05:18.580
Do you have all your limbs?!

05:18.580 --> 05:21.520
Dad, quit blowing things out of proportion.

05:21.520 --> 05:24.160
I'm fine. I only twisted my leg a little.

05:24.160 --> 05:25.990
I-It's not my fault.

05:26.390 --> 05:28.210
I'm just glad you're all right.

05:28.210 --> 05:31.950
My heart almost stopped when I heard that you were hurt.

05:32.660 --> 05:33.550
You scoundrel!

05:33.550 --> 05:35.510
Take your busy hands off of my daughter!

05:35.510 --> 05:36.590
How rude!

05:36.590 --> 05:39.510
Itou carried me all the way from school...

05:38.080 --> 05:39.510
Get down from there!

05:39.510 --> 05:40.630
Fine.

05:41.540 --> 05:43.180
I'll make the introductions.

05:43.180 --> 05:45.810
This is Itou. We go to the same school.

05:45.810 --> 05:46.500
Hi there.

05:46.500 --> 05:48.510
And this is Mitsuhashi.

05:49.550 --> 05:51.000
So this is Mitsuhashi?

05:51.000 --> 05:53.220
I will not give my Riko to the likes of you!

05:53.220 --> 05:57.930
Who's this old geeze? Thinks he can eyefuck me like that?

05:58.950 --> 06:01.350
What are you two doing?

06:03.020 --> 06:05.740
But he was eyeing me like I owe him something.

06:05.740 --> 06:07.940
Don't treat him like some hoodlum!

06:07.940 --> 06:10.290
That man is my father, you know!

06:10.750 --> 06:11.570
Got you!

06:13.030 --> 06:14.490
Shoot!

06:15.860 --> 06:17.790
Don't know what you're smoking,

06:17.790 --> 06:21.080
but you gotta wake up pretty early before you can pull a sneak—

06:22.390 --> 06:23.960
What the hell's your problem, old man?!

06:23.960 --> 06:25.470
It's the way we fight.

06:25.470 --> 06:26.260
What?

06:26.260 --> 06:30.150
You prepare for battle the moment you pass through our gates.

06:30.150 --> 06:32.180
It is <i>your fault for standing unprepared.</i>

06:32.180 --> 06:35.390
You... wrinkled old fart!

06:36.370 --> 06:38.600
What? Do you object?

06:39.620 --> 06:42.040
Stop this, I mean it!

06:44.310 --> 06:48.280
My old man says he's not done talking.

06:48.280 --> 06:49.730
Oh, so you say.

06:49.730 --> 06:51.000
Excuse me.

07:08.510 --> 07:10.470
Who's <i>that kid?</i>

07:11.030 --> 07:14.900
He's the son of Kurosaki, a man who runs a karate dojo near here.

07:14.900 --> 07:15.830
Kurosaki?

07:15.830 --> 07:17.660
He's a no-good thug.

07:18.760 --> 07:20.600
You know him, Ryou?

07:20.600 --> 07:23.430
He's a member of the Buna High crew.

07:23.430 --> 07:28.610
I heard they use their karate training to extort money from grade school kids.

07:28.610 --> 07:31.820
He's not fit to stand upwind of a true martial artist!

07:33.620 --> 07:35.130
Christ, again?

07:35.130 --> 07:40.090
You always wanna play hero whenever you hear those stories, Itou.

07:40.090 --> 07:43.290
Anyway, it doesn't got crap to do with us.

07:45.130 --> 07:47.840
Wh-What? I won't let that go unanswered!

07:47.840 --> 07:49.510
Then you accept?

07:49.510 --> 07:50.050
Of course I do!

07:50.520 --> 07:53.140
I accept your challenge! I will not stand for your insolence!

07:53.140 --> 07:55.440
Then it's settled.

07:55.440 --> 08:00.590
Whoever loses the contest next Sunday will formally take down his dojo sign.

08:00.590 --> 08:01.770
Do we have a deal,

08:02.200 --> 08:03.060
Mr. Akasaka?

08:03.060 --> 08:04.230
It will be my pleasure!

08:04.540 --> 08:06.390
Then I will take my leave.

08:37.510 --> 08:39.680
What's Mitsuhashi doing?

08:39.680 --> 08:42.590
I think he likes that bamboo clacker.

08:42.590 --> 08:44.030
He's just like a kid.

08:44.030 --> 08:45.950
Itou!

08:46.930 --> 08:47.980
What, Mitsuhashi?

08:47.980 --> 08:49.940
Hey, come here for a sec!

08:50.380 --> 08:52.050
Geez, what now?

08:52.050 --> 08:53.870
Three, don't break anything!

08:53.870 --> 08:55.400
That thing's also expensive!

08:55.400 --> 08:57.220
What is it, Mitsuhashi?

08:57.220 --> 08:58.350
Check this thing here!

08:58.350 --> 08:59.300
Huh, where?

08:59.300 --> 09:00.370
Right here!

09:01.330 --> 09:02.660
Here!

09:04.450 --> 09:06.390
Sucker!

09:07.330 --> 09:10.250
I got you! I got you good! Whatta maroon!

09:10.250 --> 09:13.000
You and your stupid, fucking tricks!

09:13.000 --> 09:15.150
But you're the one who fell for it, stupid!

09:15.150 --> 09:16.390
What the...

09:16.390 --> 09:19.720
Looks like the "notorious duo" ain't nothing to worry about.

09:21.010 --> 09:24.210
You're Mitsuhashi and Itou of Nanyou, aren't you?

09:24.210 --> 09:28.440
I thought you guys'd be badasses, but you're just a couple of clowns.

09:28.440 --> 09:29.940
You say something, asshole?

09:29.940 --> 09:32.290
You better shut up before I send you home crying.

09:32.290 --> 09:37.900
Some karate-ass punk who shakes down school kids isn't even on our level.

09:38.790 --> 09:40.770
Look who's talking.

09:40.770 --> 09:44.370
I hear you guys fight so dirty you put mud wrestlers to shame.

09:44.800 --> 09:49.330
Which means you guys'll just lose if you play by the rules, eh?

09:49.680 --> 09:52.750
Shithead! Anything goes long as you win!

09:52.750 --> 09:56.100
Mitsuhashi, hush. You aren't convincing anyone.

09:57.120 --> 10:00.930
Hey, karate boy! I don't know what you heard or where you heard it,

10:01.410 --> 10:07.250
but Itou Shinji has never once used unfair means to win fights!

10:07.250 --> 10:09.940
Yeah, but you usually get your ass kicked.

10:09.940 --> 10:11.150
I told you to shut up!

10:12.170 --> 10:13.140
Fine, I'm game.

10:13.140 --> 10:14.770
Why don't we settle up right here?

10:14.770 --> 10:15.890
Tetsuya!

10:16.670 --> 10:18.900
What're you doing? We're leaving.

10:18.900 --> 10:20.440
Sure, Dad!

10:21.600 --> 10:25.060
If you don't want me talking shit about you, then you better beat me,

10:25.060 --> 10:27.320
in a formal match, that is.

10:27.320 --> 10:29.820
I'll take you on any time, any day.

10:38.760 --> 10:41.590
So is he down with the plan, Dad?

10:41.590 --> 10:44.720
Yes. It will be a five-on-five contest.

10:45.360 --> 10:48.430
So I trust I have nothing to worry about, Tetsuya?

10:48.430 --> 10:50.570
You can trust me.

10:50.570 --> 10:55.690
Even if those two clowns show up, I can easily smack them down in tournament play.

10:56.420 --> 11:00.950
This'll be a good chance for me to beat their asses and gain some major rep.

11:04.450 --> 11:04.490
AKASAKA
DOJO

11:05.250 --> 11:07.080
What was that?

11:07.080 --> 11:11.620
Why did you promise to take down our sign if we lose?!

11:11.620 --> 11:14.580
Well, you see... it was at the heat of the moment...

11:14.580 --> 11:17.090
Don't make important decisions like that!

11:17.570 --> 11:20.390
How on earth will these kids win against them?

11:20.390 --> 11:22.930
You need to think through these things clearly!

11:22.930 --> 11:24.270
Understood.

11:24.270 --> 11:26.220
However, at the time...

11:26.220 --> 11:30.770
I see, so you accept your eventual defeat.

11:30.770 --> 11:33.770
You have no faith in the students you instruct.

11:33.770 --> 11:35.050
You're afraid.

11:35.050 --> 11:38.730
So this is the true face of Akasaka Dojo, is it not?

11:39.230 --> 11:40.560
Let's do this, Dad!

11:40.560 --> 11:42.860
We'll crush Kurosaki Dojo to smithereens!

11:42.860 --> 11:44.810
Are you with me? Are you?

11:44.810 --> 11:46.190
Like father, like daughter.

11:46.190 --> 11:46.910
Yep.

11:47.270 --> 11:50.650
So there you have it. We have no choice but to play them.

11:50.650 --> 11:52.260
There's no turning back.

11:52.260 --> 11:55.430
Wait! I, Tanaka Ryou, will do everything I can to help!

11:55.430 --> 11:57.240
Oh, Ryou, you'll fight for us?

11:57.240 --> 11:57.750
Yes!

11:57.750 --> 12:00.380
Great! That makes one for the loser column!

12:00.380 --> 12:01.640
Mitsuhashi!

12:01.640 --> 12:02.980
Silence, outsider!

12:02.980 --> 12:05.970
Those who won't fight have no right to complain!

12:05.970 --> 12:08.510
May I fight in the contest?

12:09.250 --> 12:11.100
Really, Itou? Can you do that?

12:11.100 --> 12:14.380
Of course. I don't like that guy anyway.

12:14.380 --> 12:15.060
Hey now...

12:15.420 --> 12:16.730
Itou...

12:16.730 --> 12:19.020
Master, now we have two!

12:19.800 --> 12:23.210
But it's just two. It's nowhere near enough.

12:23.210 --> 12:27.800
Screw it. I guess the super-elite Mitsuhashi will...

12:27.800 --> 12:30.240
Relax, we don't need you.

12:30.580 --> 12:34.130
You'll only ruin the contest if we let you join.

12:34.130 --> 12:37.090
Besides, I have a secret weapon.

12:37.090 --> 12:38.950
A secret weapon? What's that?

12:38.950 --> 12:39.890
It's me!

12:43.220 --> 12:44.510
You're kidding!

12:46.800 --> 12:49.270
As of yesterday, Akasaka Dojo...

12:50.430 --> 12:55.520
has a new member, the all-
powerful ringer Imai Katsutoshi.

12:55.940 --> 12:58.790
Why's that dumbass Imai here of all places?

12:58.790 --> 13:00.190
That's because...

13:00.680 --> 13:02.460
Ever since he got dumped by Misako,

13:02.460 --> 13:07.470
he decided that Riko's the only one for him, and I got dragged along.

13:07.470 --> 13:10.440
Not that I care, but when the hell did you show up?

13:12.240 --> 13:13.160
Riko.

13:13.160 --> 13:14.700
Y-Yes?

13:18.760 --> 13:23.340
I, Imai Katsutoshi, have joined this dojo just for the chance to be near you.

13:23.950 --> 13:25.450
Oops, did I say that?

13:25.450 --> 13:26.680
Yo, Pops!

13:26.680 --> 13:29.180
You may know this already, but this guy is a total moron!

13:29.180 --> 13:30.050
Hey, Mitsuhashi!

13:30.520 --> 13:32.760
You outsiders should get lost!

13:32.760 --> 13:35.500
But you <i>are</i> a moron, moron!

13:35.500 --> 13:37.030
Who're you calling a moron?!

13:37.030 --> 13:38.270
You, goddammit!

13:38.270 --> 13:40.230
Stop it, you two!

13:40.230 --> 13:41.550
Oh, Misako?!

13:41.550 --> 13:42.360
Where?

13:45.480 --> 13:47.200
What're you doing, you jerk?!

13:47.780 --> 13:50.480
You'll pay for this, jerkass!

13:51.980 --> 13:54.090
Now <i>that's a reaction.</i>

13:54.090 --> 13:56.380
You sure he's your secret weapon, old man?

13:56.380 --> 13:59.460
Shut up! I'd rather have him than you any day!

13:59.460 --> 14:02.580
But you still have only four players.

14:02.580 --> 14:03.920
You need one more.

14:03.920 --> 14:06.130
I... I still have Riko.

14:06.130 --> 14:08.430
Riko? You're crazy!

14:08.430 --> 14:09.880
I'll do it.

14:10.430 --> 14:14.010
I'm going to inherit the Akasaka dojo one day.

14:14.010 --> 14:16.850
It's only natural that I enter this match.

14:16.850 --> 14:19.020
B-But you hurt your leg.

14:19.020 --> 14:21.810
Relax. It's nothing to worry about.

14:22.160 --> 14:26.540
Unlike your brand of fighting, aikido doesn't rely on strength to win.

14:26.540 --> 14:27.850
Do you understand, hoodlum?

14:27.850 --> 14:30.320
Dad, you didn't have to say the last part!

14:30.730 --> 14:32.470
Oh, is that right?

14:32.470 --> 14:34.330
Okay, I wish y'all the best of luck!

14:34.330 --> 14:36.200
Bye now!

14:36.980 --> 14:38.100
Mitsuhashi!

14:40.000 --> 14:41.180
Three...

14:50.310 --> 14:52.520
Shouldn't you be practicing?

14:52.520 --> 14:55.060
I'll only be hurting them if I tried copying their moves.

14:55.060 --> 14:56.970
I'll be using my own style.

14:57.300 --> 14:58.450
I see.

14:59.780 --> 15:00.900
Itou.

15:01.890 --> 15:03.440
Be sure to win the match.

15:03.910 --> 15:05.430
Do it for Riko.

15:05.990 --> 15:07.980
But don't take things too far.

15:09.260 --> 15:10.680
Can you do that for me?

15:13.040 --> 15:13.990
Kyouko...

15:25.920 --> 15:29.600
I think there's something going on between those two.

15:29.600 --> 15:33.170
Putting that aside, why are <i>you blushing, Imai?</i>

15:33.170 --> 15:34.270
All right!

15:34.270 --> 15:36.750
I'll win the match, and Riko's heart as well!

15:38.160 --> 15:40.970
We still have to work for it. Let's go!

15:40.970 --> 15:42.570
T-Tanigawa! Wait!

15:42.570 --> 15:44.070
Whoops!

15:49.440 --> 15:49.480
AKASAKA
DOJO

15:58.520 --> 16:00.620
What's with you, Ryou? Get up!

16:00.620 --> 16:01.950
Uh, right.

16:02.670 --> 16:03.920
Let's go again!

16:10.250 --> 16:11.010
Riko!

16:11.800 --> 16:13.220
Are you okay, Riko?!

16:14.760 --> 16:16.180
I... I'm fine!

16:16.180 --> 16:18.220
We'll win, Ryou! I know it!

16:18.220 --> 16:19.360
Me too!

16:19.360 --> 16:20.970
Let's go again!

16:19.840 --> 16:20.800
PEACE ABOVE ALL

16:23.560 --> 16:25.220
Again!

16:38.780 --> 16:38.820
AKASAKA
DOJO

16:47.620 --> 16:47.660
Kurosaki

16:47.620 --> 16:47.660
First
Kurosaki
Tetsuya

16:47.620 --> 16:47.660
Second
Takeuchi
Hideyuki

16:47.620 --> 16:47.660
Third
Futamura
Yoshiaki

16:47.620 --> 16:47.660
Vice Captain
Suzuki
Kazuhiro

16:47.620 --> 16:47.660
Captain
Morita
Keiji

17:07.310 --> 17:11.080
What do you know? Mitsuhashi actually showed up.

17:11.080 --> 17:13.610
There's no way he'd miss this.

17:13.610 --> 17:17.780
Bastard! He's not here to play the hero, is he?

17:17.780 --> 17:19.820
Let's make sure we don't give him that chance.

17:19.820 --> 17:20.740
Yeah!

17:31.140 --> 17:35.210
We will now begin the contest between the Kurosaki and Akasaka dojos!

17:35.560 --> 17:37.020
In this line tournament,

17:37.020 --> 17:41.400
any surrender or instance where both
shoulders touch the mat will count as a loss.

17:41.400 --> 17:43.620
Those are the rules.

17:43.620 --> 17:45.430
First players forward!

17:46.060 --> 17:48.520
Tetsuya, you sure you wanna go first?

17:48.520 --> 17:51.640
Sure I'm sure. You guys take it easy.

17:51.640 --> 17:54.190
I'll take care of those bitches myself.

17:56.550 --> 17:57.730
Tanigawa.

17:58.720 --> 18:01.240
Good luck out there. Don't get hurt.

18:01.810 --> 18:03.410
R-Riko...

18:05.200 --> 18:09.170
La-di-da-di-daaa!

18:10.310 --> 18:11.400
Watch me!

18:11.400 --> 18:16.740
I, Tanigawa, will lay down my life for you and the Akasaka dojo!

18:21.140 --> 18:23.000
Well ain't that dandy?!

18:23.000 --> 18:26.350
You even got to hold her hand!

18:26.780 --> 18:28.130
S-Sorry, I wasn't thinking!

18:28.130 --> 18:29.540
Whatever, just get out there!

18:29.540 --> 18:30.530
R-Right!

18:31.520 --> 18:32.510
God!

18:32.510 --> 18:36.280
<i>I never got to hold Riko's hand.</i>

18:33.160 --> 18:34.060
Begin!

18:35.290 --> 18:36.120
Kurosaki!

18:36.120 --> 18:37.810
Hell's yeah!

18:36.280 --> 18:38.860
Darn it, I'm so jealous of that guy!

18:38.860 --> 18:41.250
I thought I told you to go, Tanigawa!

18:41.250 --> 18:43.690
Sorry, I lost.

18:44.510 --> 18:45.180
Already?

18:45.180 --> 18:45.530
Next!

18:46.740 --> 18:48.120
Second player forward!

18:48.440 --> 18:49.610
Christ!

18:49.610 --> 18:53.010
Even puppies put up more of a fight!

18:54.080 --> 18:56.850
You dumb bastard!

18:56.850 --> 18:59.050
Think you're all that, huh?

18:59.050 --> 18:59.840
However!

19:00.210 --> 19:01.860
It ends here.

19:01.860 --> 19:07.290
You'll soon find yourself at my feet begging for mercy.

19:07.290 --> 19:09.140
Imai, good luck!

19:09.140 --> 19:11.810
Gee, thanks!

19:13.600 --> 19:15.610
What? What'd I do?

19:16.070 --> 19:18.340
God, why're they playing that dumbass?!

19:18.340 --> 19:21.430
Come on, I know you're worried about them, Mitsuhashi.

19:22.000 --> 19:24.280
What the hell, you too?

19:24.280 --> 19:27.450
I only came here to see their sorry asses lose!

19:27.450 --> 19:28.120
Sure, whatever.

19:28.120 --> 19:29.460
I mean it!

19:29.460 --> 19:30.910
Both players forward!

19:31.660 --> 19:34.400
Come on, quit dicking around!

19:39.380 --> 19:41.340
Shut your fucking piehole, shorty!

19:42.540 --> 19:45.310
Just ‘cause you're taller doesn't mean shit.

19:45.310 --> 19:49.560
You heard the saying, "The bigger
they are, the smaller their brains"?

19:50.250 --> 19:53.640
Here's another saying, and it goes like this:

19:53.640 --> 19:57.280
"A small man's superior intelligence won't help him in a fight."

20:00.060 --> 20:01.400
What's with you guys?

20:01.400 --> 20:03.430
Was I not supposed to say that?

20:03.430 --> 20:03.950
Huh?

20:03.950 --> 20:06.410
That's enough! Now begin!

20:06.410 --> 20:07.780
You fucking amateur!

20:15.260 --> 20:17.080
Is that all you got?

20:17.080 --> 20:18.130
What?

20:20.740 --> 20:21.800
Shoot, did I miss him?

20:22.230 --> 20:24.220
What is he? A gorilla?

20:24.220 --> 20:27.520
Tetsuya, you need to focus! That's Beni High's boss!

20:27.520 --> 20:29.010
I know that!

20:30.430 --> 20:32.880
Dunno where you picked up those hick moves,

20:32.880 --> 20:37.200
but I've been toughened by the streets, so they're useless against me.

20:37.200 --> 20:39.980
Yay! Yay! That was awesome, Imai!

20:39.980 --> 20:43.440
You don't get your ass whupped constantly for nothing!

20:43.440 --> 20:45.490
Shaddap, Mitsuhashi!

20:50.450 --> 20:52.200
Didn't feel a thing!

20:54.120 --> 20:55.080
Die!

20:57.140 --> 20:58.730
Bastard! Get back here!

20:58.730 --> 20:59.750
Wait!

21:02.700 --> 21:05.300
He's out of bounds. Return to your positions.

21:09.010 --> 21:11.860
What the hell! Can't you be flexible, Pops?!

21:11.860 --> 21:14.320
Nobody gives a damn about "out of bounds"!

21:14.320 --> 21:15.710
This isn't a street fight.

21:15.710 --> 21:19.460
You keep up that Pollyanna BS, you're gonna lose!

21:19.460 --> 21:21.700
God, you shoulda put me in...

21:20.750 --> 21:21.700
Shut up, you fool!

21:21.700 --> 21:23.550
Geez, begin already!

21:24.150 --> 21:25.360
Imai!

21:24.150 --> 21:25.360
Behind you!

21:27.570 --> 21:28.360
Imai!

21:42.200 --> 21:43.740
K-Kurosaki!

21:44.590 --> 21:48.070
What the hell was that? He totally had his back turned!

21:48.070 --> 21:51.760
He restarted the match. It was his fault for not paying attention.

21:51.760 --> 21:52.970
Say what?

21:52.970 --> 21:54.560
Isn't that right, Mr. Akasaka?

21:55.140 --> 21:55.880
Yes.

21:56.430 --> 21:57.520
Th-That's low!

21:57.350 --> 21:57.390
Third
Tanaka Ryou

21:57.350 --> 21:57.390
Second
Imai Katsutoshi

21:57.350 --> 21:57.390
First
Tanigawa Yasuo

22:04.690 --> 22:07.150
Next up: third player, Tanaka Ryou.

22:08.740 --> 22:09.360
Coming!

22:09.360 --> 22:11.230
Ryou, focus!

22:11.230 --> 22:12.320
Keep your cool.

22:13.520 --> 22:15.450
Don't worry! I'll win!

22:18.770 --> 22:20.250
Bow to each other!

22:22.790 --> 22:26.930
I'll show that rude twerp what true martial arts looks like!

22:27.710 --> 22:29.280
I got no time for wimps.

22:29.280 --> 22:33.180
I'm gonna lay out Nanyou's Itou, and gain some major rep.

22:33.180 --> 22:34.220
Begin!

22:40.230 --> 22:41.770
Fucking runt.

22:44.630 --> 22:46.280
Don't rely on strength.

22:47.030 --> 22:48.690
Avoid the fist, get behind him...

22:49.900 --> 22:51.490
And attack!

22:52.020 --> 22:52.990
Winner...

22:57.270 --> 22:59.540
Y... You stupid kid!

23:03.020 --> 23:04.040
Ryou!

23:04.460 --> 23:06.880
That dumbass! He got caught slipping!

23:13.250 --> 23:14.470
We're waiting, ref!

23:18.210 --> 23:19.640
Winner, Kurosaki!

23:28.990 --> 23:30.160
Riko...

23:31.970 --> 23:35.630
If this were an official match, Ryou would have won.

23:39.580 --> 23:41.210
I'm going to do it.

23:41.210 --> 23:42.330
I <i>will win!</i>

23:42.780 --> 23:44.790
For everyone.

23:44.620 --> 23:44.660
Kurosaki

23:44.620 --> 23:44.660
First
Kurosaki
Tetsuya

23:44.620 --> 23:44.660
Second
Takeuchi
Hideyuki

23:44.620 --> 23:44.660
Third
Futamura
Yoshiaki

23:44.620 --> 23:44.660
Vice Captain
Suzuki
Kazuhiro

23:44.620 --> 23:44.660
Captain
Morita
Keiji

23:52.720 --> 23:55.220
What's your plan now, Mr. Akasaka?

23:56.210 --> 23:57.590
What are you saying?

23:57.590 --> 24:02.520
Why don't you man up and admit your defeat before you embarrass yourself even further?

24:02.940 --> 24:03.950
Out of the question!

24:03.950 --> 24:06.810
This contest isn't over! We will continue!

24:07.950 --> 24:09.080
Is that so?

24:09.080 --> 24:14.530
Then I will referee the remaining matches as per our agreement.

24:15.260 --> 24:17.490
We got this! They're too easy!

24:20.030 --> 24:20.900
Yo!

24:23.290 --> 24:26.710
What's with the hard look you got on, Itou?

24:27.100 --> 24:30.460
Mitsuhashi, if you're here to joke around, save it.

24:30.460 --> 24:32.260
I'm really not in the mood.

24:32.590 --> 24:34.070
Ooh, scary.

24:34.070 --> 24:37.640
You always take things too serious, Itou.

24:37.640 --> 24:39.270
Fine by me, though.

24:39.270 --> 24:42.850
You better drop all five of ‘em on their asses, you heard?

24:42.850 --> 24:44.610
You're damn right I will.

24:44.610 --> 24:46.060
Just leave them to me.

24:46.810 --> 24:48.930
Both players forward!

24:52.560 --> 24:55.990
So I finally get to meet Nanyou's all mighty Itou.

24:58.950 --> 25:00.750
Bow to each other!

25:01.570 --> 25:03.160
Itou, good luck!

25:09.390 --> 25:10.290
Now begin!

25:15.970 --> 25:18.930
Yeah, Itou! Get him! Kick his ass!

25:18.930 --> 25:20.100
Damn!

25:20.100 --> 25:22.730
Nanyou's Itou sure lives up to his rep!

25:22.730 --> 25:26.400
Yeah, and I heard he stomps around with an unbeatable blond guy...

25:26.400 --> 25:27.390
Blond guy?!

25:27.390 --> 25:30.110
Get him! Kick 'im in the balls!

25:30.110 --> 25:31.690
I-Is that Mitsuhashi?!

25:38.170 --> 25:39.660
Who's this dude?

25:40.860 --> 25:41.870
You bastard!

25:41.870 --> 25:44.530
Wh-What the hell's your fucking problem?

25:44.530 --> 25:46.580
This ain't a fistfight; it's a contest!

25:47.750 --> 25:50.920
Does that mean you should fight dirty, huh?

25:52.290 --> 25:56.640
If you're into martial arts, then fight me like a man!

25:56.640 --> 25:58.010
Come on, Kurosaki!

25:59.150 --> 26:03.720
Hey, what's got you heated? What did I ever do to you?

26:03.720 --> 26:05.090
Shut up!

26:05.090 --> 26:09.060
Seeing you and your pops grinds my gears!

26:11.480 --> 26:14.440
Itou! Itou! Go get him!

26:14.440 --> 26:16.850
Keep it up! Take him down!

26:14.820 --> 26:16.850
Itou! You're doing good!

26:16.850 --> 26:18.170
You're doing great, Itou!

26:16.850 --> 26:18.150
Keep punching him!

26:18.170 --> 26:20.170
Your lines may be cheesy, but you still kick ass!

26:20.170 --> 26:22.160
What are you doing? Get out of bounds!

26:24.490 --> 26:25.300
Wait!

26:25.950 --> 26:27.280
He's out of bounds!

26:27.280 --> 26:31.080
Mr. Kurosaki! The referee is not supposed to instruct a contestant!

26:31.080 --> 26:33.820
Yeah! Yeah! That's a loss by penalty!

26:33.820 --> 26:35.140
Itou wins this! Itou wins!

26:35.140 --> 26:36.790
Mitsuhashi, shut up!

26:37.320 --> 26:40.430
I'll win once I pound him flat on the ground!

26:40.430 --> 26:42.970
Return to your starting positions!

26:49.080 --> 26:49.890
Begin.

26:53.330 --> 26:54.950
Itou, relax.

26:54.950 --> 26:55.520
Right.

26:57.480 --> 26:58.690
Itou!

27:04.990 --> 27:05.780
Itou!

27:05.780 --> 27:06.450
Itou!

27:06.450 --> 27:07.830
Referee, that was a foul!

27:08.240 --> 27:10.760
How was that a foul? Eh, ref?

27:11.340 --> 27:13.520
I've already restarted the match.

27:13.520 --> 27:15.790
I-I didn't hear you say anything!

27:16.110 --> 27:19.050
Honestly, you too, Mr. Akasaka?

27:19.050 --> 27:22.510
Are you making false accusations because all hope is lost?

27:23.500 --> 27:25.520
N-No I am not!

27:25.520 --> 27:26.850
But I clearly didn't...

27:26.850 --> 27:30.050
I attacked once I heard him say "begin."

27:30.050 --> 27:32.830
My fingers got his eyes purely by accident, not on purpose.

27:32.830 --> 27:34.400
You heard him.

27:35.570 --> 27:38.110
Fine. Let's continue the matches.

27:39.340 --> 27:42.320
I can take on five players myself.

27:43.200 --> 27:44.030
Riko.

27:44.030 --> 27:45.870
No, Riko... I can still...

27:45.870 --> 27:46.960
No.

27:46.960 --> 27:49.850
Akasaka Dojo must now save face.

27:49.850 --> 27:52.450
Sorry to do this to you, but this is now my fight.

27:53.760 --> 27:54.740
This is nothing.

27:54.740 --> 27:57.170
Your next opponent is me.

28:00.980 --> 28:03.470
Are you crazy, Three? I'm
supposed to be the captain!

28:03.470 --> 28:05.430
God, what's with you people?

28:05.430 --> 28:07.220
All injured parties should get off the damn mat!

28:07.220 --> 28:09.370
Outsiders shouldn't interfere!

28:09.370 --> 28:11.600
This isn't a street fight! This is a match!

28:11.600 --> 28:14.400
He's right! You have no business doing anything!

28:14.400 --> 28:17.560
Mitsuhashi, you're only going to screw everything up.

28:17.560 --> 28:20.920
Shut the hell up! Can't you fucking read?

28:22.270 --> 28:22.320
Akasaka

28:22.270 --> 28:22.320
First
Tanigawa
Yasuo

28:22.270 --> 28:22.320
Second
Imai
Katsutoshi

28:22.270 --> 28:22.320
Third
Tanaka
Ryo

28:22.270 --> 28:22.320
Vice Captain
Itou
Shinji

28:22.270 --> 28:22.320
Captain
Akasaka
Riko

28:22.270 --> 28:22.320
Captain
Mitsuhashi
Takashi

28:26.660 --> 28:28.230
When did he...

28:28.230 --> 28:29.950
Don't, Mitsuhashi!

28:30.350 --> 28:31.960
Relax, let me handle it.

28:31.960 --> 28:34.870
Hey, blondie! I won't allow it!

28:34.870 --> 28:37.710
You wanna lose your fucking dojo?!

28:38.310 --> 28:39.510
And there you have it.

28:39.510 --> 28:41.920
I will be your next opponent.

28:41.920 --> 28:46.230
Are you just waltzing in just to show off, you hoodlum?

28:46.230 --> 28:47.930
Get lost, shithead!

28:49.460 --> 28:51.810
Yes, I <i>am a hoodlum.</i>

28:51.810 --> 28:55.910
But I ain't like a father-son team who cheats in competitions.

28:55.910 --> 28:58.180
Or do I got you punks shook?!

28:59.090 --> 29:00.680
N-No I ain't!

29:00.680 --> 29:02.150
C'mon, let's fight!

29:02.700 --> 29:04.110
Now you're talking.

29:09.790 --> 29:10.780
What the hell?

29:10.780 --> 29:13.320
I never know what you hoodlums are thinking!

29:14.500 --> 29:18.160
Well, not like I expect your monkey ass to comprehend.

29:19.220 --> 29:21.960
Lissen up! This is what I'm doing!

29:21.960 --> 29:22.500
What?

29:26.090 --> 29:26.880
Three!

29:30.880 --> 29:31.890
What are you doing?!

29:34.850 --> 29:36.850
C'mon! Fucking die already!

29:36.850 --> 29:40.310
Dumb piece of shit! Mark-ass bitch! Your shit's garbage!

29:40.310 --> 29:43.660
You ain't never bringing game to me in ten goddamn centuries!

29:43.660 --> 29:45.860
You get me, punk motherfucker? You get me?!

29:46.200 --> 29:47.160
That bastard!

29:47.160 --> 29:48.030
Let's rush him!

29:51.530 --> 29:52.450
You punks...

29:52.880 --> 29:54.640
best back the fuck up!

29:57.540 --> 29:59.920
I'm clearing out all you cocksuckers!

29:59.920 --> 30:02.630
Here's my Bamboo Clacker!

30:08.760 --> 30:10.470
What are you doing?!

30:17.930 --> 30:18.980
Dammit!

30:18.680 --> 30:18.720
PEACE ABOVE ALL

30:23.260 --> 30:24.460
I fucking won!

30:24.460 --> 30:26.390
Did your bitch-made asses see that?!

30:26.390 --> 30:29.400
Ch'all better recognize my awesomeness!

30:32.950 --> 30:37.090
What'cha say, Pops?! You sorry you didn't put me in the first time?!

30:37.090 --> 30:38.420
You lose.

30:38.420 --> 30:39.950
You're damn right! I lose—

30:39.950 --> 30:41.330
What?

30:41.330 --> 30:42.460
Why the hell?

30:42.460 --> 30:43.600
You lose by penalty.

30:43.600 --> 30:46.170
I thought the rules said anything goes!

30:46.480 --> 30:48.590
You're not allowed to use weapons!

30:50.740 --> 30:53.600
You inflexible old geeze!

30:53.430 --> 30:53.470
PEACE ABOVE ALL

30:53.600 --> 30:58.200
Mr. Akasaka, I'll have you take down your sign.

31:07.020 --> 31:07.060
AKASAKA
DOJO

31:18.950 --> 31:20.790
Cheer up, Pops!

31:20.790 --> 31:23.500
Who cares about one or two old dojos anyway?

31:23.500 --> 31:25.280
I do, you dolt!

31:25.280 --> 31:27.720
What? It ain't my fault!

31:27.720 --> 31:30.300
It's all because of these weakass bitches!

31:30.610 --> 31:32.280
Who the fuck you calling bitches?

31:32.280 --> 31:34.690
We put our asses on the line!

31:34.690 --> 31:37.760
This is your goddamn fault! Everything's your goddamn fault!

31:37.760 --> 31:41.520
Everything went to shit once you stepped in, fucking prick!

31:41.770 --> 31:44.730
Y'all couldn't beat a one of 'em, so shut the fuck up!

31:46.800 --> 31:47.690
Fine.

31:55.030 --> 31:55.070
AKASAKA
DOJO

32:03.380 --> 32:04.620
Mr. Akasaka,

32:04.620 --> 32:08.580
the results may be unexpected, but a promise is a promise.

32:08.580 --> 32:11.580
Now bring down your sign.

32:16.050 --> 32:21.560
If you're not willing to do it yourself, then perhaps I'll lend a hand.

32:28.980 --> 32:33.950
So all's we got to do is lower the sign and we're good, old man Kurosaki?

32:33.950 --> 32:37.230
Of course, that is what we agreed on.

32:37.230 --> 32:37.660
Good.

32:38.100 --> 32:42.300
Since I'm supposedly responsible for this outcome, I will...

32:42.300 --> 32:43.370
lower the sign!

32:43.370 --> 32:47.300
Whoever lowers the sign is none of my concern.

32:52.630 --> 32:52.670
AKASAKA
DOJO

33:25.960 --> 33:27.670
The sign is now lower!

33:37.630 --> 33:38.940
Mr. Akasaka?

33:40.630 --> 33:42.860
Did <i>you think of this?</i>

33:42.860 --> 33:44.220
You dumbfuck!

33:44.220 --> 33:45.830
I thought it up!

33:45.830 --> 33:46.780
Nice, ain't it?!

33:46.770 --> 33:52.090
*Character of the eponymous anime who relies on his cleverness to solve problems.

33:46.780 --> 33:49.640
I'm the Ikkyu-san* of Nanyou High!

33:52.090 --> 33:56.970
Well, if this doesn't shame you, we can call this a wash.

33:56.970 --> 33:59.270
<i>If this doesn't shame you.</i>

34:01.240 --> 34:03.200
Tetsuya, we're leaving.

34:03.200 --> 34:04.390
Hold it!

34:05.830 --> 34:09.670
I <i>will take you on again one of these days.</i>

34:09.670 --> 34:15.630
I don't like losses by penalties. I don't like losses period!

34:16.530 --> 34:18.140
Once I heal up, okay?

34:18.140 --> 34:19.030
Hoodlum!

34:19.030 --> 34:22.010
Tetsuya, just ignore him. God!

34:27.600 --> 34:29.530
Cheer up, Pops!

34:29.530 --> 34:32.210
Aren't you glad you didn't lose your dojo?

34:32.210 --> 34:35.000
So, do you see me in a different light now?

34:35.000 --> 34:36.700
You're a genius, Three!

34:39.350 --> 34:40.530
Mitsuhashi!

34:40.530 --> 34:44.240
Mark my words. You'll never, ever<i> have my daughter!</i>

35:13.360 --> 35:15.440
Let's worry about the future tomorrow.

35:15.440 --> 35:18.030
When tomorrow comes, it'll all work out.

35:21.450 --> 35:23.490
If it doesn't work out, I'll just run away.

35:23.490 --> 35:26.030
If I'm found, I'll make up an excuse.

35:29.450 --> 35:31.460
You and me are friends, partner.

35:31.460 --> 35:33.210
If the going gets tough, the tough say goodbye.

35:37.420 --> 35:39.510
I help you.

35:38.340 --> 35:39.510
We're family.

35:39.510 --> 35:41.510
I like you.

35:53.440 --> 35:55.400
On stressful days, I'll hit you.

35:55.400 --> 35:58.230
Then, I'll say, "I'm sorry," and you'll forgive me.

36:01.320 --> 36:02.860
That cute girl is mine,

36:02.860 --> 36:05.990
but I belong to no one.

36:09.410 --> 36:11.410
We're all brothers and sisters in this world.

36:11.410 --> 36:13.370
When the going gets tough, the tough kick and scream.

37:15.540 --> 37:17.090
See you next time!
